1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,229
On Linux, install Sforzando first.
Plogue offers it as a beta.

2
00:00:06,429 --> 00:00:12,871
Unzip it and run install_sforzando.sh,
without sudo: it asks for your password.

3
00:00:16,071 --> 00:00:20,586
Now run the MIDI-GPT installer
from the release zip.

4
00:00:20,786 --> 00:00:25,943
Answer y so it can close REAPER
while it installs extensions.

5
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:35,514
Sforzando's VST3 lives in /usr/lib/vst3,
which REAPER doesn't scan by default.

6
00:00:35,714 --> 00:00:41,157
The installer adds that folder to
REAPER's plug-in paths for you.

7
00:00:43,357 --> 00:00:47,229
Answer y to download
the Arachno SoundFont.

8
00:00:49,429 --> 00:00:54,443
In REAPER, Sforzando's VST3
now shows up in the FX browser.

9
00:00:54,643 --> 00:01:00,514
On minimal systems, Sforzando also
needs: sudo apt install libxcb-util1
